  "original_brief": "Show a reusable fabric shopping bag upright with two handles and a few purchased items peeking above the opening. Make the flexible sides and carrying handles clearly distinct from a rigid shopping basket. Reject a backpack, paper-only carrier definition, wheeled trolley, or decorative gift bag that obscures the intended shopping use.",
  "accepted_brief": "Show a plain open retail shopping bag upright in a three-quarter view, with a tall solid-sided body, two separate loop handles and a visible opening. Preserve the inspected 3dicons dynamic color source. Keep the tall solid body and paired loops visually distinct from the accepted squat slotted shopping basket. Exclude wheels, backpack straps, a closed top, a bow, a gift tag, tissue paper and gift-specific decoration. The illustration does not narrow the definition to a particular material or require visible contents.",
  "image_visually_accepted": true,
  "production_integrated": false,
  "definition_unchanged": "A bag used to carry purchased items.",
  "observations": [
    "At native comparison size the solid tall body, near and far loop handles, and dark open cavity remain visible.",
    "The bag is distinct from the accepted squat slotted basket through silhouette and handle construction, independent of orange versus green color.",
    "All five Match pair tints, focused and settled, leave the bag and basket outlines and openings visible; numbered badges do not cover the identifying cues.",
    "Memory unmatched and generic-check matched states preserve the same cues at current full opacity.",
    "The separately labeled 0.68 stress rows are lighter but preserve the body and opening. They are not current caller presentation.",
    "The original source, 414x512 crop and native captures show no gift tag, bow, branding or decorative fill."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "An empty generic bag cannot prove shopping use independently of context; gift bags may share this form.",
    "Fabric, flexibility and visible purchases from the old brief are not depicted and are not claimed. The accepted broader carrier definition is unchanged.",
    "This is an AI visual/editorial decision at the captured component sizes, not human participant recognition or responsive full-board acceptance.",
    "No source model or animation was acquired. No audio was played, changed or newly approved.",
    "Production image metadata, final packaging and persisted delivery still require a separate scoped implementation and verification."
  ],
